data-lazy=\"false\" data-src=\"https://store.bblcdn.com/s1/default/81d6c63baf64464e89b76046c7724490/B-XA006-1.png\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMjQiIGhlaWdodD0iMjQiIHZpZXdCb3g9IjAgMCAyNCAyNCIgZmlsbD0ibm9uZSIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj4KPHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjI0IiBoZWlnaHQ9IjI0IiBmaWxsPSIjRkZGRkZGIi8+Cjwvc3ZnPgo=\"/></div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"border: 1px solid #cccccc; padding: 10px; height: 50px;\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 19px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border: 1px solid #cccccc; padding: 10px; height: 50px;\">\n<div class=\"hover-img-container\">\n<p style=\"margin: 0;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong><a href=\"../../products/mini-screwdriver-toolkit\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #00ae46;\" target=\"_blank\">Mini Screw Driver Tools Kit - QA025</a></strong></span></p>\n<img class=\"hover-img product-desc-lazy-media product-desc-lazy-media--image bg-bbl-white animate-pulse max-h-[400px]\" data-lazy=\"false\" data-src=\"https://store.bblcdn.com/s7/default/97b388a5a3a84dceb5c0cdb1e717ca2e/tool2.png\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMjQiIGhlaWdodD0iMjQiIHZpZXdCb3g9IjAgMCAyNCAyNCIgZmlsbD0ibm9uZSIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj4KPHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjI0IiBoZWlnaHQ9IjI0IiBmaWxsPSIjRkZGRkZGIi8+Cjwvc3ZnPgo=\"/></div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"border: 1px solid #cccccc; padding: 10px; height: 50px;\">Gift</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_tpc-ic\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\" style=\"margin-top: 30px; font-size: 24px;\">Documentation</h2>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_tpc-ic\">\n<div class=\"pct_t-p\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\" style=\"font-size: 24px; margin-top: 40px; text-align: center;\">Important Notices</h2>\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-size: 20px; text-align: left;\">Core Safety Rules</h2>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">This product is intended for users aged 14 and above. Users under the age of 14 must be under direct adult supervision throughout use.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>DO NOT</strong> touch the moving parts while the device is operating to prevent pinching injuries.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Please use only official tools for any firmware operations. Flashing with third-party tools is not supported and may cause irreversible damage, which is not covered by warranty.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Before use, inspect all 3D-printed parts and sand down any sharp edges or burrs if present. Store the model and small parts in a location out of reach of children and pets to prevent choking hazards.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-size: 20px; text-align: left;\">Warning of Lithium Battery</h2>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">This product utilizes a replaceable rechargeable lithium battery.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Adult supervision is required when children are handling batteries or the charger. Do not operate the product while it is charging.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Ensure the battery is installed correctly. Improper installation may result in short circuits, overheating, or potential explosion.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Regularly inspect the charger’s cord, plug, housing, and other components for damage. If any damage is found, discontinue use immediately until the device is fully repaired.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Choking Hazard: Contains small parts; not suitable for children under 3 years of age.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Improper disposal of this product may harm the environment - please recycle responsibly.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-size: 20px; text-align: left;\">Charging Precautions</h2>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Use only the officially supplied charger. The charger is not a toy.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">The USB charger for this product only supports standard 5V 1-2A input. Please always use the original charger that meets the voltage/current requirements, or charge directly via a computer USB port. <strong>DO NOT</strong> use chargers with output higher than 5V or 2A (such as mobile fast chargers, 9V/12V adapters, etc.), as this may cause device damage, overheating, or even serious fire hazards.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>DO NOT</strong> cover the device while charging, and keep it away from high temperature, humidity, or flammable environments. Never charge the device unattended.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>DO NOT</strong> charge the battery pack if it is overheating. Allow it to cool down completely before recharging.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">If the battery pack or charger becomes wet, ensure they are thoroughly dry before attempting to charge.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-size: 20px; text-align: left;\">Lithium Battery Safety Precautions</h2>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>DO NOT</strong> attempt to use or charge the battery pack if it shows any signs of leakage or corrosion.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>DO NOT</strong> disassemble, crush, or mechanically abuse the battery pack.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\"><strong>DO NOT</strong> dispose of the battery pack in fire.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">Exercise extreme caution when handling an overheated battery pack.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
  "description_text": "Four-wheel drive gives the CyberBrick 4WD Car the grip to feel like a real RC build, not a shelf model. Its compact layout is designed for faster, more responsive driving than the earlier 4x4 Mini Off-Roader platform.\n\nDouble wishbone independent suspension helps each wheel react cleanly over uneven surfaces. That means better control, smoother movement, and a more satisfying build for anyone who cares about mechanics.\n\nSeparate headlight and indicator control adds a more realistic driving feel after assembly. Use the recommended transparent PETG lighting profile to get the clearest effect from the CyberBrick LEDs.\n\n*The following is the App connection of CyberBrick Official SoccerBot as an example, which is similar to this model.\n\nThis product is intended for users aged 14 and above. Users under the age of 14 must be under direct adult supervision throughout use.\n\nDO NOT touch the moving parts while the device is operating to prevent pinching injuries.\n\nPlease use only official tools for any firmware operations. Flashing with third-party tools is not supported and may cause irreversible damage, which is not covered by warranty.\n\nBefore use, inspect all 3D-printed parts and sand down any sharp edges or burrs if present. Store the model and small parts in a location out of reach of children and pets to prevent choking hazards.\n\nThis product utilizes a replaceable rechargeable lithium battery.\n\nAdult supervision is required when children are handling batteries or the charger. Do not operate the product while it is charging.\n\nEnsure the battery is installed correctly. Improper installation may result in short circuits, overheating, or potential explosion.\n\nRegularly inspect the charger’s cord, plug, housing, and other components for damage. If any damage is found, discontinue use immediately until the device is fully repaired.\n\nChoking Hazard: Contains small parts; not suitable for children under 3 years of age.\n\nImproper disposal of this product may harm the environment - please recycle responsibly.\n\nUse only the officially supplied charger. The charger is not a toy.\n\nThe USB charger for this product only supports standard 5V 1-2A input. Please always use the original charger that meets the voltage/current requirements, or charge directly via a computer USB port. DO NOT use chargers with output higher than 5V or 2A (such as mobile fast chargers, 9V/12V adapters, etc.), as this may cause device damage, overheating, or even serious fire hazards.\n\nDO NOT cover the device while charging, and keep it away from high temperature, humidity, or flammable environments. Never charge the device unattended.\n\nDO NOT charge the battery pack if it is overheating. Allow it to cool down completely before recharging.\n\nIf the battery pack or charger becomes wet, ensure they are thoroughly dry before attempting to charge.\n\nDO NOT attempt to use or charge the battery pack if it shows any signs of leakage or corrosion.\n\nDO NOT disassemble, crush, or mechanically abuse the battery pack.\n\nDO NOT dispose of the battery pack in fire.\n\nExercise extreme caution when handling an overheated battery pack.",
